items.promptMarkdown:
A dispatcher edits a draft before saving it, and the original order changes too.

```js
const draft = { ...order };
draft.reference = 'DR-77';
draft.customer.city = 'Ashfield';

order.reference;      // unchanged
order.customer.city;  // 'Ashfield'
```

Why does one assignment leak into `order` and the other does not?

solution.code:
function cityOf(order) {
  const address = order && order.shippingAddress;
  const city = address && address.city;
  if (typeof city === 'string' && city.trim() !== '') {
    return city;
  }
  return 'unknown';
}

grading.starterCode:
function cityOf(order) {
  // Assumes every order has an address with a city.
  return order.shippingAddress.city;
}

