  // Edits the caller's tickets, and ignores the cap.
  tickets.forEach(ticket => {
    ticket.priority = ticket.priority + 1;
  });
  return tickets;
}

items.promptMarkdown:
A report page shows anonymised orders. After viewing the report, the operator's own order list shows every customer as "Redacted".

```js
function anonymise(orders) {
  return orders.map((order) => {
    order.customerName = 'Redacted';
    return order;
  });
}
```

The author points out that `map` returns a new array and never modifies the one you called it on. Are they right, and what is the defect?

